description:
pkix-lint/src/deviation.rs DeviationRunner::run_chain (lines 743-755):

    let mut result = DeviationRunResult::default();
    for (i, cert) in chain.iter().enumerate() {
        ...
        let partial = self.apply_deviations(raw, cert, now_unix);
        result.findings.extend(partial.findings);
        result.deviated.extend(partial.deviated);
    }

apply_deviations returns a fresh DeviationRunResult on each iteration, which is then immediately extended into the outer result. This means:
1. Two Vec allocations per iteration (partial.findings, partial.deviated).
2. Two extend calls per iteration, copying elements.

A better pattern: have apply_deviations accept &mut DeviationRunResult and push directly into the caller's Vecs, eliminating the intermediate allocation entirely.

Alternatively, pre-size with_capacity based on chain.len() * runner.lints().len().

Category: R5 (unnecessary intermediate Vec allocation in hot path)
